    "procedure": [
      "Retrieve the completed development archive through a private catalog. A gzip tar requires one sequential compressed-stream read (about 102 MB); only the 21 named members need to be retained on disk (about 0.92 MB plus metadata).",
      "Compute the full compressed-archive SHA-256 during transfer and record it; the existing one-byte receipt establishes only presence, size, and ETag.",
      "Accept only the exact allowlisted regular-file members; reject path traversal or duplicate members. Load NPY with allow_pickle=False, preserve uint8 RGB and float32 numeric arrays, and check dtype, shape, and records.digest(array) against every recorded reference. Also record each extracted file SHA-256.",
      "Retain only the three selected accepted request/proposal records and matching provider rows, with hashes of their full source files. Reconstruct request observations from the selected condition arrays and verify observation IDs, condition IDs, request fingerprints, actual model, and raw provider/proposal equality.",
      "Re-encode each accepted controller action chunk with the unchanged pinned ActionAdapter and require agreement with its saved full [1,10,32] encoded endpoint before any GPU solve. Keep saved latent and first-generation endpoint only as N100 reproduction references."
    ]
